---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="How a Community Got Clean Water — The Mar Azul and ASADA Santa Marta Story | Coyol Real Estate"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <!-- SEO Meta Tags -->
    <meta name="description" content="In 2016, Barrio Los Ángeles had no public water. Wells were contaminated, children were getting sick. This is the documented story of how that changed." />
    <meta name="keywords" content="Mar Azul, ASADA Santa Marta, Nosara water infrastructure, Barrio Los Angeles, Costa Rica community development, well GA-334, AYA approval, Rivera Norte" />
    
    <!-- Open Graph / Facebook -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="How a Community Got Clean Water" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="In 2016, families in Barrio Los Ángeles had no public water. Wells were contaminated. This is the documented story of how that changed." />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://coyolnosara.com/images/mar-azul/water/hero.jpg" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://coyolnosara.com/blog/mar-azul-water-donation-asada-santa-marta" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Coyol Real Estate" />
    
    <!-- Twitter -->
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="How a Community Got Clean Water" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="In 2016, families in Barrio Los Ángeles had no public water. This is the documented story of how that changed." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://coyolnosara.com/images/mar-azul/water/hero.jpg" />
    
    <!-- Canonical URL -->
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://coyolnosara.com/blog/mar-azul-water-donation-asada-santa-marta" />
    
    <!-- Article Schema -->
    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "How a Community Got Clean Water — The Mar Azul and ASADA Santa Marta Story",
      "description": "The documented story of how Barrio Los Ángeles went from contaminated wells to clean drinking water.",
      "image": "https://coyolnosara.com/images/mar-azul/water/hero.jpg",
      "datePublished": "2026-08-07",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Coyol Real Estate"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Coyol Real Estate",
        "url": "https://coyolnosara.com"
      },
      "mainEntityOfPage": {
        "@type": "WebPage",
        "@id": "https://coyolnosara.com/blog/mar-azul-water-donation-asada-santa-marta"
      },
      "keywords": ["Mar Azul", "ASADA Santa Marta", "Nosara", "water infrastructure", "Barrio Los Angeles"]
    }
    </script>
  </Fragment>

  <article class="blog-post">
    <!-- HERO SECTION -->
    <section class="hero">
      <img src="/images/mar-azul/water/hero.jpg" alt="Water infrastructure serving ASADA Santa Marta" class="hero-image" onerror="this.parentElement.classList.add('no-image')" />
      <div class="hero-overlay">
        <p class="hero-category">Investigation</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title">How a Community<br>Got Clean Water</h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- INTRO -->
    <section class="intro">
      <p class="lead">In January 2016, a geologist walked through Barrio Los Ángeles documenting 32 hand-dug wells. Most had less than 30 centimeters of water. Many were contaminated. Families were bathing in the river. Children were getting sick.</p>
      
      <p>Ten years later, those same families have clean drinking water flowing from their taps. This is the documented story of how that happened.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- THE CRISIS -->
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>The Crisis: January 2016</h2>
      
      <p>Barrio Los Ángeles sits on the north bank of the Nosara River. For generations, the community had no public water service — not from ASADA Nosara, not from ASADA Santa Marta, not from AyA. Every family dug their own well.</p>
      
      <p>On January 31, 2016, consulting geologist José Vargas Gutiérrez (registration CGCR-180) conducted a formal census of wells in the community. What he found was alarming.</p>
      
      <div class="document-box">
        <p class="document-title">From the Geological Report — February 2016</p>
        <blockquote>
          "The sanitary condition of practically all the wells is alarming. Due to the small size of the properties, the distance to septic tanks or their drainage does not meet minimum recommendations — most of these structures are located between 5 and 20 meters from the well openings."
        </blockquote>
        <p class="document-source">— José Vargas Gutiérrez, Consulting Geologist (CGCR-180)</p>
      </div>
      
      <p>The report documented over 30 wells with water tables between 4 and 30 centimeters. Several wells had been abandoned after owners confirmed contamination — bad smell, bad taste, stomach illnesses. Residents shared water between family members when one well ran dry, carried water in buckets and bottles, and bathed in the river.</p>
      
      <p>The situation had multiple causes: the CNE's construction of a flood control dike along the Nosara River (built by JCB Construcciones S.A.) had deepened the riverbed and waterproofed the banks, lowering the water table. An earthquake had raised the coastal land. Years of El Niño drought had depleted what remained.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- THE COMMITTEE -->
    <section class="content-section alternate">
      <h2>The Committee</h2>
      
      <p>The geological study wasn't commissioned by the government. It was requested by a community committee organized to solve the problem themselves.</p>
      
      <p>The committee's approach was practical: join ASADA Santa Marta, which had few users and operational capacity, and fund the infrastructure needed to extend service to Barrio Los Ángeles. Neighbors volunteered to donate land and contribute financially toward drilling a deep well that would become ASADA property.</p>
      
      <p>Among those on the committee was Marion Peri, who would later develop the Mar Azul and Nosara Hills projects in the hills above the community.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- THE WELL -->
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>The Well: March 2021</h2>
      
      <p>On March 8, 2021, Perforaciones Jiménez y Delgado issued invoice #148 for the drilling of a deep well at Santa Marta. The well would be registered as GA-334 with the National Groundwater Registry.</p>
      
      <div class="data-card">
        <div class="data-row">
          <span class="data-label">Well Registration</span>
          <span class="data-value">GA-334</span>
        </div>
        <div class="data-row">
          <span class="data-label">Drilling Contractor</span>
          <span class="data-value">Perforaciones Jiménez y Delgado Ltda.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="data-row">
          <span class="data-label">Invoice Number</span>
          <span class="data-value">#148</span>
        </div>
        <div class="data-row">
          <span class="data-label">Cost</span>
          <span class="data-value">₡5,424,000</span>
        </div>
        <div class="data-row">
          <span class="data-label">Paid By</span>
          <span class="data-value">Nosara Constructions and Development Group Ltda.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="data-row">
          <span class="data-label">Property Transfer</span>
          <span class="data-value">Donated to ASADA Santa Marta</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <p>The well was drilled at an elevation of 35 meters above sea level. Testing confirmed a yield of 3.23 liters per second — enough to supply hundreds of families.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- AYA APPROVAL -->
    <section class="content-section alternate">
      <h2>Official Approval: June 2025</h2>
      
      <p>On June 25, 2025, Oscar Ampié Bermúdez of AyA's Rural Aqueduct Management Unit (UEN Gestión de Acueductos Rurales) issued Report No. GSD-UEN-GAR-2025-02417. The technical study for connecting Nosara Hills and Mar Azul through ASADA Santa Marta was formally approved.</p>
      
      <div class="document-box">
        <p class="document-title">From AYA Report GSD-UEN-GAR-2025-02417</p>
        <blockquote>
          "The ASADA Santa Marta de Nicoya currently has 406 services with 100% metering... The proposal is that from well 2 (GA-334), potable water can be supplied to the Nosara Hills and Mar Azul projects through macroflow meters installed at the entrance of each project."
        </blockquote>
        <p class="document-source">— Oscar Ampié Bermúdez, UEN Gestión de Acueductos Rurales, AyA</p>
      </div>
      
      <p>The same well that was funded by private developers in 2021 is now part of an integrated system serving over 400 connections, with capacity for 86 more — 46 for Nosara Hills and 40 for Mar Azul.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- THE INFRASTRUCTURE TODAY -->
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>The System Today</h2>
      
      <p>ASADA Santa Marta now operates a network of six registered wells with a combined capacity of over 10 liters per second. The system includes a 400-cubic-meter concrete storage tank at 95 meters elevation. All 406 active connections are metered.</p>
      
      <div class="stats-grid">
        <div class="stat-card">
          <span class="stat-number">406</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Active Connections</span>
          <p class="stat-detail">100% metered service</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card">
          <span class="stat-number">6</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Registered Wells</span>
          <p class="stat-detail">Documented with MINAE</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card">
          <span class="stat-number">400m³</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Storage Capacity</span>
          <p class="stat-detail">Concrete tank at 95m elevation</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card">
          <span class="stat-number">10+ l/s</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Combined Yield</span>
          <p class="stat-detail">From all water sources</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <p>The water sources are registered with MINAE under authorization DA-1363-2021-AGUAS-MINAE, expediente 686-R. ASADA Santa Marta holds an official delegation agreement (convenio de delegación) with AyA.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- WHAT THE DOCUMENTS SHOW -->
    <section class="content-section alternate">
      <h2>What the Documents Show</h2>
      
      <p>This isn't a story that requires interpretation. The paper trail is clear:</p>
      
      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
          <div class="timeline-content">
            <span class="timeline-date">January 31, 2016</span>
            <p>Geologist José Vargas Gutiérrez documents contaminated wells and water crisis in Barrio Los Ángeles. Report requested by community water committee.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
          <div class="timeline-content">
            <span class="timeline-date">March 8, 2021</span>
            <p>Perforaciones Jiménez y Delgado drills well GA-334. Invoice #148 for ₡5,424,000 paid by Nosara Constructions and Development Group. Well donated to ASADA Santa Marta.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
          <div class="timeline-content">
            <span class="timeline-date">2021</span>
            <p>Water sources registered with MINAE under DA-1363-2021-AGUAS-MINAE.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
          <div class="timeline-content">
            <span class="timeline-date">June 25, 2025</span>
            <p>AyA approves technical study (Report GSD-UEN-GAR-2025-02417) for connecting Nosara Hills and Mar Azul via ASADA Santa Marta. System now serves 406 metered connections.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CLOSING -->
    <section class="closing-section">
      <p>In Barrio Los Ángeles, children no longer drink from contaminated wells. Families no longer bathe in the river. The taps work.</p>
      
      <p>Not because of a government program that arrived after decades of waiting. Because a community organized, a developer invested, and the infrastructure was built.</p>
      
      <p>The documents are public record. The well is pumping. The water is clean.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- FOOTER -->
    <footer class="post-footer">
      <div class="documents-note">
        <p><strong>Source Documents:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Geological Report, José Vargas Gutiérrez (CGCR-180), February 2016</li>
          <li>Invoice #148, Perforaciones Jiménez y Delgado Ltda., March 8, 2021</li>
          <li>AyA Technical Report GSD-UEN-GAR-2025-02417, June 25, 2025</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      
      <div class="tags">
        <span>Tags:</span>
        <span class="tag">Investigation</span>
        <span class="tag">Mar Azul</span>
        <span class="tag">ASADA Santa Marta</span>
        <span class="tag">Barrio Los Ángeles</span>
        <span class="tag">Water Infrastructure</span>
        <span class="tag">Nosara</span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* RESET & BASE */
  .blog-post {
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  /* HERO */
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    height: 70vh;
    min-height: 500px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #1a1a1a;
  }

  .hero.no-image .hero-overlay {
    background: none;
  }

  .hero-image {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .hero-overlay {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    padding: 4rem;
    background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(0,0,0,0.8) 0%, transparent 100%);
    color: white;
  }

  .hero-category {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 3px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .hero-title {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 3.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  /* INTRO */
  .intro {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 2rem 3rem;
  }

  .intro .lead {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .intro p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #444;
  }

  /* CONTENT SECTIONS */
  .content-section {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
  }

  .content-section.alternate {
    max-width: 100%;
    background: #f7f7f5;
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
  }

  .content-section.alternate h2,
  .content-section.alternate p,
  .content-section.alternate .document-box,
  .content-section.alternate .timeline {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: #1a1a1a;
  }

  .content-section p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    color: #333;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  /* DOCUMENT BOX */
  .document-box {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 2rem;
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
    border-left: 3px solid #333;
  }

  .content-section.alternate .document-box {
    background: white;
  }

  .document-title {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #666;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .document-box blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: none;
    background: none;
  }

  .document-box blockquote p {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #333;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .document-source {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #666;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* DATA CARD */
  .data-card {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    background: #f7f7f5;
    border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
  }

  .data-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
  }

  .data-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .data-label {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #666;
  }

  .data-value {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    text-align: right;
  }

  /* STATS GRID */
  .stats-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .stat-card {
    background: #f7f7f5;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
  }

  .stat-number {
    display: block;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .stat-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #666;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .stat-detail {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: #999;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* TIMELINE */
  .timeline {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .timeline-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .timeline-marker {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    background: #333;
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .timeline-content {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .timeline-date {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #666;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .timeline-content p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #333;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* CLOSING */
  .closing-section {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
  }

  .closing-section p {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #333;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .closing-section p:last-child {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #1a1a1a;
  }

  /* FOOTER */
  .post-footer {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
  }

  .documents-note {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #f7f7f5;
  }

  .documents-note p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: #333;
  }

  .documents-note ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .documents-note li {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #666;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .tags > span:first-child {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }

  .tag {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: #666;
    background: #f0f0f0;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  /* RESPONSIVE */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .stats-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .hero {
      height: 50vh;
    }

    .hero-title {
      font-size: 2.5rem;
    }

    .hero-overlay {
      padding: 2rem;
    }

    .intro .lead {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
    }

    .content-section h2 {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .stats-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .data-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.25rem;
    }

    .data-value {
      text-align: left;
    }
  }

  /* Hide floating buttons */
  :global(.fixed) {
    display: none !important;
  }
</style>
